      "justification": "End-tidal CO2 monitoring provides real-time feedback on CPR quality (target ETCO2 >10 mmHg indicates adequate compression) and serves as an early indicator of return of spontaneous circulation (ROSC). This is recommended in ACLS guidelines during cardiac arrest management."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "continue_high_quality_cpr",
      "timestamp_minutes": 30.0,
      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "Mandatory per AHA ACLS guidelines for cardiac arrest - high-quality CPR must be maintained continuously to preserve perfusion during resuscitation."
    },
